but my heart
wished to hear, and to loose me I bade my companions,
nodding with my brows;

You, on the one hand, with oars the deep surf of the salt-sea
strike, sitting upon the rowing-benches, if somehow Zeus
may grant this destruction to flee from and to escape;

But I, having put on my famous armour, and two spears
long, taking in my hands, onto the decking of the ship I stepped,
the prow’s;

Truly, whenever she vomited it out, like a cauldron on a great fire
all of her would seethe up with a roar, churned, and on high the spray
on the tops of the crags, on both, would fall;

And looking to the swift ship and at the same time among my companions
already of them I perceived the feet and hands above
being lifted high;

But when we had fled the rocks and dread Charybdis
and Scylla, at once then to the god’s blameless island
we came;

Then indeed I, while still on the open-sea, being in the black ship,
heard the lowing of cattle lodging in the yard
and the bleating of sheep;
